      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T01:07:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason of putting it in pkvm_vm structure is to get rid of the lock when getting the pkvm_vcpu (in `get_pkvm_vcpu`). Otherwise, we need to hold the lock first to get a pkvm_vcpu from pkvm_vm first, then play with the atomic reference counter. Doing so with holding a lock seems like making the atomic reference count meaningless. So putting the atomic reference counters in pkvm_vm.",
      "parentUuid": "14d74f29_a469ba30",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 88,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "0614d355879a522356094e367a4e49d946c47bfa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d226b4b2_65a1e0e5",
