      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T13:12:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ahh ok got it. But now when I think about it, I feel this reference count mechanism is not serving its purpose fully. If a detach is called while some one has taken a refcount, detach returns NULL and the vcpu will not be freed I think. Would that be a problem? If we are sure that detach will be the last operation and no reference count would exist at that time, then its okay. But then, do we really need a refcount in that case?\n\nIMHO It should be the put_vcpu function that should free the resource when refcount is zero. detach could do the detach operation and decrement the refcount. Since detach would reset the vcpus[handle] to NULL, no further get_pkvm_vcpu will succeed and last put operation can free the vcpu gracefully.\n\nI do not have a full background of the issue and might be missing something. Just thinking out loud :-)",
      "parentUuid": "ec89131c_32892f62",
